@14 = ~Enable BG2-style HLAs in IWDEE~
@15 = ~Without Rogue Rebalancing Thief HLA Revisions~
@16 = ~With Rogue Rebalancing Thief HLA Revisions~
@17 = ~Rogue Rebalancing Thief HLA resources are already present. Do not install this variant on top of another installation of RR Thief HLA Revisions.~
@18 = ~KITLIST.2DA or LUABBR.2DA is missing; the active Thief HLA tables cannot be discovered safely.~
@19 = ~One or more core IWDEE Thief HLA resources required by the Rogue Rebalancing revision are missing.~
@95 = ~WARNING: A discovered Thief HLA table did not contain the columns required for safe HLA patching and was left unchanged.~
@96 = ~WARNING: Scribe Scrolls was found in a Thief HLA table with a nonstandard prerequisite. It was preserved rather than forcing Crippling Strike over another mod's design.~
@97 = ~Epic Thieving-style Set Traps scaling was detected. Set Death Trap and the tiered Exploding Trap damage/radius progression are preserved; Exploding Trap receives Rogue Rebalancing-compatible secondary-effect saves and large/heavy-creature exclusions, while the remaining RR Thief HLA revisions (including Time Trap -> Acid Trap) are applied.~
@98 = ~Set Exploding Trap

With this ability, the character can set a deadly trap that explodes when an enemy comes near. The trap grows more powerful with the character's Set Traps skill and can only be triggered by enemies. A successful Save vs. Breath reduces the fire damage by half and avoids the knockback/knockdown effects. Exceptionally large or heavy creatures (Dragons, Giants, Stone and Iron Golems) are immune to the knockback/knockdown effects but still take fire damage.
  Set Traps 0-149: Deals 10d6 fire damage to all enemies within 15 feet (Save vs. Breath for half).
  Set Traps 150-199: Deals 12d6 fire damage to all enemies within 20 feet (Save vs. Breath at -1 for half).
  Set Traps 200-249: Deals 14d6 fire damage to all enemies within 25 feet (Save vs. Breath at -2 for half).
  Set Traps 250 and above: Deals 16d6 fire damage to all enemies within 30 feet (Save vs. Breath at -3 for half).

Although the radius of the explosion grows as the trap gets more powerful, the proximity needed to trigger the trap does not change.~
@99 = ~WARNING: Epic Thieving-style Exploding Trap resources were detected, but their installed secondary-effect structure did not match the supported one-Wing-Buffet/one-knockdown layout. The Set Traps scaling resources were preserved without forcing the RR secondary-effect compatibility patch.~

